.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- move files using colon-path atomic names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE DEST
.br
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE
\&...
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR mv (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation rewrites path arguments,
creates missing parent directories for destinations, and performs the move.
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B mv
from
.B PATH
instead.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7)
for
.BR BASE:LEAF
syntax.
.PP
When the destination is a directory (or multiple sources are given), each
source is placed at
.I DEST/LEAF
where
.I LEAF
is the atomic name of the source (the part after
.BR : ,
or the basename if no colon-path was used).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a/b:c/d ../x
Runs
.B mv a/b/c/d ../x/c/d
after creating
.BR ../x/c .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the planned command without executing it.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backup[=CONTROL]
Make a backup of each existing destination file.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Do not prompt before overwriting.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Prompt before overwrite.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-clobber
Do not overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target\-directory=DIR
Move all sources into
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-no\-target\-directory
Treat
.I DEST
as a normal file.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update[=WHEN]
Move only when
.I SOURCE
is newer (or destination is missing).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Explain what is being done.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-suffix=SUFFIX
Override the usual backup suffix.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-trailing\-slashes
Remove trailing slashes from each
.IR SOURCE .
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\-context
Set SELinux context of destination to default.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation.
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-mv\fR → \fBmv\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR colon-path (7),
.BR colon-cp (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
